# Functions

Functions are declared using the `func` keyword. Functions need to declare the types of all their arguments and return values.
As in the Go programming language, types are declared after the names of the arguments.

In the example, `addReshape` takes two arguments, `a` and `b`, both of type `[2][3]float32`, and returns a single value of type `[3][2]float32`.

